 333:source\asw/sound.c **** /**
 334:source\asw/sound.c ****  * \brief Timer interrupt body: output one sample, swap buffers when needed (N1, N3, N4).
 335:source\asw/sound.c ****  *
 336:source\asw/sound.c ****  * Per tick exactly one of: output a sample (volume scaled), swap + SetEvent(tsk_reader,
 337:source\asw/sound.c ****  * ev_BufEmpty), or count an underrun. Does nothing while the dual buffer path is off.
 338:source\asw/sound.c ****  *
 339:source\asw/sound.c ****  * Call only from ISR2(isr_Timer).
 340:source\asw/sound.c ****  *
 341:source\asw/sound.c ****  * \return RC_SUCCESS when a sample was output, a swap was done or the dual buffer path is off,
 342:source\asw/sound.c ****  *         RC_ERROR_BUFFER_EMTPY when this tick was an underrun (reader late, last value held, N9)
 343:source\asw/sound.c ****  */
